WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:06.639
On Tuesday afternoon Daisy and Kaleem were going to visit Scamp.

2
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.977
"I'm coming with you," Beatrice said.

3
00:00:09.978 --> 00:00:12.728
"I need to keep an eye on you."

4
00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:16.131
"Huh? What do you mean?" Daisy asked.

5
00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:20.923
"Um, just so you're safe," Beatrice said.

6
00:00:20.924 --> 00:00:26.394
Daisy shrugged. "Grace will be there. So you're going to have to be careful."

7
00:00:26.395 --> 00:00:29.329
Beatrice landed on Daisy's headband.

8
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:33.088
"Kaleem said I look like his mother's pin, remember?

9
00:00:33.089 --> 00:00:39.815
So I'll stay right here. If Grace notices me, tell her I'm just a decoration."

10
00:00:39.816 --> 00:00:43.384
"Okay, but make sure you stay very still.

11
00:00:43.385 --> 00:00:54.154
Pins don't usually move—or buzz either!"

12
00:00:54.155 --> 00:00:58.318
The kids walked Scamp and fed him.

13
00:00:58.319 --> 00:01:04.939
They also refilled his pool.

14
00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:13.372
Scamp barked, splashing around happily. "I love playing in the water!"

15
00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:19.764
Grace looked worried. "He keeps barking. Do you think he's lonely?"

16
00:01:19.765 --> 00:01:24.302
"He's happy to be in the water," Daisy said. "He loves—"

17
00:01:24.303 --> 00:01:28.417
"Bzz!" Beatrice made a warning sound.

18
00:01:28.418 --> 00:01:31.204
"I'm thirsty," Kaleem said quickly.

19
00:01:31.205 --> 00:01:33.256
"Let's go get milkshakes."

20
00:01:33.257 --> 00:01:35.135
Grace looked disappointed.

21
00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:39.389
"That sounds fun. But I can't go.

22
00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.846
I have to clean the filter on my fish tank."

23
00:01:42.847 --> 00:01:46.763
"I never knew owning fish was so complicated," Kaleem said.

24
00:01:46.764 --> 00:02:00.574
Grace sighed. "It's a big responsibility. Sometimes there's too much to do."

25
00:02:00.575 --> 00:02:12.585
She said good-bye, and Daisy and Kaleem set off for the ice cream parlor.

26
00:02:12.586 --> 00:02:16.011
Halfway there, they saw a rabbit running down the sidewalk.

27
00:02:16.012 --> 00:02:18.971
She looked terrified.

28
00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.333
"What's wrong?" Daisy called.

29
00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:24.944
The rabbit skidded to a stop.

30
00:02:24.945 --> 00:02:32.456
"I just saw a monster! It roared like a horrible, angry beast!"

31
00:02:32.457 --> 00:02:35.817
A bird swooped close to Daisy.

32
00:02:35.818 --> 00:02:38.653
"You're the girl who can talk to animals!

33
00:02:38.654 --> 00:02:43.148
We've all heard about you. I saw a monster too.

34
00:02:43.149 --> 00:02:46.421
It had shaggy fur like a bear!"

35
00:02:46.422 --> 00:02:49.560
Daisy told Kaleem what the animals had said.

36
00:02:49.561 --> 00:02:51.939
Kaleem scratched his head.

37
00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:57.394
"How strange. What do you think they saw?"

38
00:02:57.395 --> 00:03:00.942
Just then a dog barked loudly.

39
00:03:00.943 --> 00:03:04.809
"Monster! Monster!" the dog said.

40
00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:09.089
"There's a monster on the loose!"

41
00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:12.153
Daisy looked over the fence at the dog.

42
00:03:12.154 --> 00:03:15.222
"Did you see the monster that looks like a bear?"

43
00:03:15.223 --> 00:03:19.326
"I don't know what a bear is," the beagle said.

44
00:03:19.327 --> 00:03:28.627
"The monster I saw had a long, strange neck like a giant, furry snake!"

45
00:03:28.628 --> 00:03:31.308
A cat wandered past.

46
00:03:31.309 --> 00:03:34.135
"Was the monster as tall as a house?

47
00:03:34.136 --> 00:03:36.992
Because I saw that monster too.

48
00:03:36.993 --> 00:03:42.524
I've never seen anything like it!"

49
00:03:42.525 --> 00:03:46.969
A butterfly fluttered past.

50
00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.370
"Be careful!

51
00:03:48.371 --> 00:03:51.739
There's a monster around, and it shoots something out of its mouth.

52
00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:55.636
It might be poison!"

53
00:03:55.637 --> 00:03:58.786
Daisy filled in Kaleem again.

54
00:03:58.787 --> 00:04:02.995
"A monster? Here?" Kaleem said.

55
00:04:02.996 --> 00:04:07.990
"Kaleem, there's no such thing as monsters," Daisy said.

56
00:04:07.991 --> 00:04:12.859
Kaleem grinned. "I didn't believe people could talk to animals until recently.

57
00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:16.887
But now I do. Maybe monsters are real too!"

58
00:04:16.888 --> 00:04:18.478
Daisy shook her head.

59
00:04:18.479 --> 00:04:21.443
She didn't think that monsters were real.

60
00:04:21.444 --> 00:04:25.893
But she was sure the animals had seen something strange.

61
00:04:25.894 --> 00:04:29.523
"Where did you see this monster?" she asked the animals.

62
00:04:29.524 --> 00:04:33.559
"It stomped past my fence," the dog said.

63
00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:39.864
"I saw it heading that way." The cat gestured down the street.

64
00:04:39.865 --> 00:04:42.583
Daisy beckoned to Kaleem.

65
00:04:42.584 --> 00:04:50.986
"Let's go that way—and investigate!"

